{"database":{"advisory-count":1509,"last-commit":null,"last-updated":null},"lockfile":{"dependency-count":348},"settings":{"target_arch":[],"target_os":[],"severity":null,"ignore":[],"informational_warnings":["unmaintained","unsound","notice"]},"vulnerabilities":{"found":true,"count":1,"list":[{"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0204","package":"crossbeam-epoch","title":"Invalid pointer dereference in `fmt::Pointer` impl for `Atomic` and `Shared` when the underlying pointer is invalid","description":"Affected versions of `fmt::Display` dereference the underlying pointer. This causes a invalid pointer dereference e.g., when a pointer created with `Atomic::null` or `Shared::null`. `fmt::Debug` impls and pre-0.9 `fmt::Display` impls, which do not dereference pointers, are not affected by this issue.","date":"2026-07-06","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["NULL-pointer-dereference"],"cvss":null,"informational":null,"references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/crossbeam-rs/crossbeam/pull/1276","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"versions":{"patched":[">=0.9.20"],"unaffected":["<0.9.0"]},"affected":null,"package":{"name":"crossbeam-epoch","version":"0.9.18","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"5b82ac4a3c2ca9c3460964f020e1402edd5753411d7737aa39c3714ad1b5420e","dependencies":[{"name":"crossbeam-utils","version":"0.8.21","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null}}]},"warnings":{"unmaintained":[{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"unsafe-libyaml","version":"0.2.11","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"673aac59facbab8a9007c7f6108d11f63b603f7cabff99fabf650fea5c32b861","replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2024-0449","package":"unsafe-libyaml","title":"unsafe-libyaml is unmaintained","description":"The [repository](https://github.com/dtolnay/unsafe-libyaml) was archived by\nits owner on 2024-03-25 and is read-only. The last release is 0.2.11\n(March 2024).\n\n`unsafe-libyaml` is a machine translation of libyaml's C code into unsafe\nRust (c2rust). Bugs found in it will not be fixed upstream. It is used by\n`serde_yaml` (itself deprecated) and by forks such as `serde_yaml_ng`.\n\n## Alternatives\n\nConsider a YAML parser written in safe Rust, for example:\n\n- [saphyr](https://crates.io/crates/saphyr) ([serde-saphyr](https://crates.io/crates/serde-saphyr) for serde users)\n- [noyalib](https://crates.io/crates/noyalib)","date":"2024-03-25","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/dtolnay/unsafe-libyaml","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}}],"unsound":[{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"anyhow","version":"1.0.102","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"7f202df86484c868dbad7eaa557ef785d5c66295e41b460ef922eca0723b842c","replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0190","package":"anyhow","title":"Unsoundness in `Error::downcast_mut()`","description":"Affected versions of this crate violate borrow rules, resulting in undefined behavior, when the user adds context to an error via `Error::context` and then later calls `Error::downcast_mut` on the returned `Error`.\n\nThe flaw was corrected in commit `6e8c000` by revising how the mutable reference is constructed, avoiding inclusion of a shared reference in the resulting borrow chain.\n\n## Example\n\n```rust\nuse anyhow::Error;\nuse std::fmt;\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\nstruct ErrorContext(&'static str);\n\nimpl fmt::Display for ErrorContext {\n    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {\n        fmt::Display::fmt(&self.0, f)\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let mut error = Error::msg(\"inner error\").context(ErrorContext(\"old context\"));\n    let context: &mut ErrorContext = error.downcast_mut().unwrap();\n    context.0 = \"new context\";\n    println!(\"{:?}\", error);\n}\n```\n\n## Miri output\n\n```\nerror: Undefined Behavior: trying to retag from <1538> for Unique permission at alloc602[0x38], but that tag only grants SharedReadOnly permission for this location\n   --> src/ptr.rs:170:18\n    |\n170 |         unsafe { &mut *self.ptr.as_ptr() }\n    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this error occurs as part of retag at alloc602[0x38..0x48]\n    |\n    = help: this indicates a potential bug in the program: it performed an invalid operation, but the Stacked Borrows rules it violated are still experimental\n    = help: see https://github.com/rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines/blob/master/wip/stacked-borrows.md for further information\nhelp: <1538> was created by a SharedReadOnly retag at offsets [0x38..0x48]\n   --> src/ptr.rs:89:18\n    |\n 89 |             ptr: NonNull::from(ptr),\n    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    = note: stack backtrace:\n            0: anyhow::ptr::Mut::<'_, ErrorContext>::deref_mut\n                at src/ptr.rs:170:18: 170:41\n            1: anyhow::error::<impl anyhow::Error>::downcast_mut::<ErrorContext>\n                at src/error.rs:560:18: 560:46\n            2: main\n                at examples/downcast_mut.rs:15:38: 15:58\n```","date":"2026-06-25","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["memory-corruption"],"keywords":["unsound","downcast_mut"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/dtolnay/anyhow/issues/451","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":{"arch":[],"os":[],"functions":{"anyhow::Error::downcast_mut":["<1.0.103"]}},"versions":{"patched":[">=1.0.103"],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"tokio","version":"1.49.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"72a2903cd7736441aac9df9d7688bd0ce48edccaadf181c3b90be801e81d3d86","dependencies":[{"name":"bytes","version":"1.12.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.191","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"mio","version":"1.2.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"pin-project-lite","version":"0.2.17","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"socket2","version":"0.6.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"tokio-macros","version":"2.6.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"windows-sys","version":"0.61.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0386","package":"tokio","title":"`AsyncFd::new` and related constructors violate I/O safety","description":"`tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd` provides safe constructors (`new`, `with_interest`, `try_new`, and `try_with_interest`) that accept any `T: AsRawFd` rather than requiring proof of ownership or validity of the file descriptor. Because `RawFd` implements `AsRawFd`, safe code can construct an `AsyncFd` from an arbitrary or closed file descriptor, or close/replace the underlying file descriptor while the `AsyncFd` is still alive.\n\nThis violates I/O safety in two ways:\n\n1. `AsyncFd<T>` implements `AsFd` for all `T: AsRawFd` by calling `BorrowedFd::borrow_raw(self.as_raw_fd())`, allowing safe code to obtain an arbitrary `BorrowedFd<'_>` without owning the file descriptor.\n2. Tokio's I/O driver stores a pointer to an internal allocation in the `epoll`/`kqueue` user data for registered file descriptors. If the underlying file descriptor is duplicated and then closed while an `AsyncFd` is alive, and the OS reuses that file descriptor number for a another IO resource on the same runtime, dropping the first `AsyncFd` deregisters the reused file descriptor number and frees the first while the original file description remains registered in `epoll`, leading to a use-after-free when a readiness event fires.\n\nStarting in Tokio 1.51.6, 1.53.3, and 1.54.0, `AsyncFd::new`, `AsyncFd::with_interest`, `AsyncFd::try_new`, and `AsyncFd::try_with_interest` are deprecated in favor of the `unsafe` constructors `AsyncFd::register` and `AsyncFd::register_with_interest`. Callers must ensure that the file descriptor remains valid, open, and unchanged for the lifetime of the `AsyncFd`.","date":"2026-10-13","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":["memory-corruption"],"keywords":["io-safety","use-after-free"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":["https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/issues/8538","https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/issues/8539"],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8587","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":{"arch":[],"os":[],"functions":{"tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::new":[">=0.3.2"],"tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::try_new":[">=1.37.0"],"tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::try_with_interest":[">=1.37.0"],"tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd::with_interest":[">=0.3.2"]}},"versions":{"patched":[">=1.51.6, <1.52.0",">=1.53.3"],"unaffected":["<0.3.2"]}}]}}
